{"skill":{"slug":"bilibili-all-in-one","displayName":"Bilibili All In One"},"version":{"version":"1.0.24","createdAt":1777702888540,"changelog":"Version 1.0.24\n\n- Improved video/audio downloader logic in `src/downloader.py` for greater robustness and precision.\n- Refactored and enhanced utility functions in `src/utils.py` to improve maintainability and efficiency.\n- Updated `skill.json` with corresponding version and metadata adjustments.","changelogSource":"auto","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"README.md","size":17017,"sha256":"be2dc06a09668cd48d1ce283dc6a6d0385a30f6804027febc8fd4a4109464d79","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"STRUCTURE.md","size":794,"sha256":"746788f6f129ee1df11fbc14f2fa857517866c0349c63272bf0a863c5bf03b5e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"main.py","size":5372,"sha256":"687bd370db791ee5a5bd6f6616fa5204fdb6075673de5446ece0270eb40361a7","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"requirements.txt","size":83,"sha256":"0708a4e28dcc7616f1b083d8f8d3726cde05c7a5e6a641876971cb8d11f80054","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/publish.sh","size":3758,"sha256":"c739b8d18655a74e5882e9a7f97df0a962ecc62aa459ad363ead6f5fcae01b58","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill.json","size":18244,"sha256":"bef4b0f61b5a740a827250f21c5937f03bbf981e3cba0c37287ef6cab04a58c0","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"skill.md","size":21374,"sha256":"92602328d62540c6753850733f4986cb870bef5372f60cccf86a6b350dc96d5d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"src/__init__.py","size":515,"sha256":"da3198962dce28345eb200ed17e1186a9767c760737254ff835083193f840444","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/auth.py","size":11550,"sha256":"04b3cb0cdf681f54e691a8add73c6ef6734f53eda1d86da032133f8b945fb2ae","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/downloader.py","size":18913,"sha256":"254a69d15c9f08000768c251aac9c299c1c9395d5125211570b3ced5b022980d","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/hot_monitor.py","size":7391,"sha256":"3b7fc7dc4af3cb8dad5b1a92b7b23de0b73ec0e852f29649b9491ec1b7f7f6cf","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/player.py","size":12167,"sha256":"fb18175aede2ddb10c17ac79a175b99b874add6e4f706da483556ee5aae1ff4e","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/publisher.py","size":26526,"sha256":"3fd2548bb127376ece2b53b3af759639ca102154e6de5567c5b8a9f900f48ab4","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/subtitle.py","size":24254,"sha256":"73dfb3ea42d011fb65907fb71e8e93f2a922856c15547c3b949d2e750f0f46ea","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/utils.py","size":7847,"sha256":"d4ac2f350651e4f3259edf0d27b122c7c7c6cd2a4d41300795de1ae92363f7f8","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"src/watcher.py","size":9896,"sha256":"742a5d1e80d6e4c458fb8347f5d1c288fe77b0953b6c9bd87c9d0207d0a89982","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2516,"sha256":"e9f1d50f5f1dfacef4829bedb366ac6cd69a72e0e5f78d91ae58077bc55f3f33","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789177759516,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"d214e56c7e68491182494e486e5cbff561162e8501163b9fd0d848948bd66874","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/d214e56c7e68491182494e486e5cbff561162e8501163b9fd0d848948bd66874","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780086066194},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":38,"checkedAt":1789177759516},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a real Bilibili toolkit, but users should review it because full session cookies can be attached to broader network requests than the documentation promises.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill handles full browser session cookies and creates general-purpose httpx clients with those cookies and follow_redirects=True; this is broader than needed for public subtitle/stat/hot-list operations and upload-CDN transfer.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Installation is a normal pinned pip requirements install with no automatic post-install execution found. A release helper script for clawhub publish is present in the artifact but is not invoked by the skill runtime.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The docs and manifest say credentials are only sent to official Bilibili endpoints, but shared authenticated clients are injected into public/read-only modules, and subtitle download requests an API-provided URL without host validation.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Credential persistence is sensitive but disclosed and disabled by default; when enabled, the code writes .credentials.json with 0600 permissions, rejects group/world-writable directories, expires files after 30 days, and provides clear deletion methods.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The package coherently implements the stated Bilibili functions: hot lists, downloads, playback data, subtitles, and publishing. Publishing is high-impact but disclosed and guarded by dry_run=True plus confirm=True before account mutation.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable giving the skill full Bilibili session cookies. Prefer using it without credentials where possible, avoid BILIBILI_PERSIST, use a throwaway account for publishing or high-quality downloads, and run it in an isolated environment while reviewing outbound traffic.","findings":"[T09] unexpected: Accepted as a material concern: src/subtitle.py downloads target_sub['url'] through self._get_client(), while src/auth.py creates clients with full session cookies and redirects enabled. This undercuts the documented network boundary.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted as a material concern in reduced form: upload-CDN use is expected for publishing, but src/publisher.py uses the full authenticated client for CDN upload steps even though a separate X-Upos-Auth value is supplied.\n[PE3] expected: Credential handling is expected for publishing and high-quality downloads. The plaintext cookie persistence risk is real, but the artifact discloses it, defaults to memory-only storage, and implements permission and expiry checks.\n[TP4] expected: Downgraded: the full artifact includes hot_monitor, downloader, watcher, subtitle, player, and publisher modules matching the declared toolkit. The release helper script is extra developer tooling but not runtime behavior.\n[SC4] expected: Network and parsing dependencies are expected for this purpose, but pinned versions should be independently dependency-scanned and updated; this was not the deciding issue.\n[TM1] expected: Downgraded: the cited chmod text appears in warnings and protective credential-file permission checks, not tool-parameter abuse.\n[TM3] expected: Downgraded: the world/group-writable references are defensive checks that refuse unsafe credential persistence locations.\n[SQP-3] expected: Downgraded: README.md is Chinese, but skill.md includes English content and the skill metadata declares zh-CN and en.\n[LP3] expected: Partially downgraded: skill.md frontmatter does not list allowed tools, but skill.json declares network, filesystem, and subprocess scope in detail.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789177759516}}}}}